# Python bytecode / caches from running the analyzer and its tests
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Generated analyzer output for real backtest reports.
# Ad-hoc / scratch summaries are ignored, but the per-round summaries the
# automation harness commits (reports/roundNN_YYYYMMDD.summary.json), the
# per-iteration tuner summaries (reports/tuner/iterNNNN.summary.json), and the
# synthetic verification artifacts under reports/samples/ are intentionally
# kept (all negated below). Keep the negations AFTER the ignore rule.
#
# NOTE on reports/tuner/: only the .summary.json files there are force-tracked
# (they are tiny and are the permanent, complete history of every iteration).
# The full iterNNNN.html reports are NOT ignored - they stay tracked too, but
# run_tuner_loop.ps1 prunes (git rm) all but the newest N (TunerHtmlKeep, N=20
# by default) each iteration so the repo does not accumulate unbounded large
# HTML. The .summary.json files are never pruned. See automation/tuner/README.md.
reports/*.summary.json
!reports/round*.summary.json
!reports/tuner/*.summary.json
!reports/samples/*.summary.json

# Per-run logs and generated runtime tester .ini from the automation harness.
# The harness scripts and the .ini TEMPLATE stay tracked; only the logs dir is
# ignored.
automation/logs/

# Auto-tuner per-iteration logs. The tuner's state (tuner_state.json) and the
# current_params.json marker stay tracked; only the logs dir is ignored.
automation/tuner/logs/

# Large market-data artifacts. The split .zip.NNN chunks ARE tracked (they are
# the transport for the raw XAUUSD tick data, each < 100 MB). But the reassembled
# archive and the extracted multi-hundred-MB CSV must NEVER be committed - they
# are regenerated on demand from the chunks. Keep the chunks; ignore the rest.
data/joined.bin
data/*.zip
data/**/*.csv
data/*.csv

# Local compile log produced by update.bat (machine-specific, not tracked)
update_compile.log
